@implements IDisposable
@* One named area of a site's page (F117, ADR 0106): a section that must carry an id, a kicker over its content, and the
   classes a site adds for its look. The id is what the guide's ShowPage names and the section index links, so a page
   built of bands has every area named by construction, and the band puts itself on the frame's list as it draws
   (F118). The band draws no style of its own: .band and .kicker are the site's, so each site keeps its look. Its body
   lays out as if it weren't there; on a page of slides, when it holds more than a screen, the frame's module pages it
   sideways and shows the pager beside it (F118). *@
<section id="@Id" class="@Classes" data-whole="@Whole">
    <div class="band-body">
        @if (Kicker is not null)
        {
            <span class="kicker">@Kicker</span>
        }
        @ChildContent
    </div>
    <div class="band-pager" hidden>
        <button type="button" class="band-page" data-step="-1" aria-label="Previous page">‹</button>
        <span class="band-pages" aria-live="polite"></span>
        <button type="button" class="band-page" data-step="1" aria-label="Next page">›</button>
    </div>
</section>
